<title>PAKISTAN: PAKISTAN COTTON MARKET SHUT ON INDEPENDENCE DAY.</title>
<headline>PAKISTAN COTTON MARKET SHUT ON INDEPENDENCE DAY.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Karachi Cotton Association (KCA) was shut on Thursday as Pakistan celebrated its 50th independence anniversary. It will reopen on Friday.</p>
<p>Wednesday's closing spot rates of KCA in rupees per maund (37.32 kg):</p>
<p>				     Wednesday	  August 12</p>
<p>    NIAB-78 (1997/98 crop)   2,571.25	   2,588.13</p>
<p>    K-68    (1996/97 crop)   2,554.38	   2,554.38</p>
<p>    MNH-93  (1996/97 crop)   2,558.75	   2,558.75</p>
<p>($1=40.62 rupees)</p>
<p>-- Ibrahim Khan (9221) 5685192; Fax (9221) 5673428</p>
